er presents a comprehensive study of gradient-based privacy attacks in federated learning and introduces novel defense mechanisms that significantly mitigate these risks. Our adaptive gradient perturbation and adversarial training techniques offer a promising avenue for enhancing privacy without compromising model performance. Future work will explore the integration of these defenses with other privacy-preserving technologies, such as secure enclaves and blockchain-based audit trails, to further strengthen the security of collaborative learning systems. Additionally, extending the evaluation to include more diverse datasets and real-world scenarios will provide deeper insights into the generalizability and scalability of our methods.  ibliographystyle{unsrt}  ibliography{references}
